    "check.doc-references-missing.why": "Prose that names a function which is gone describes an API that no longer exists; this is the drift between documentation and code the tool is for.",
    "check.example-does-not-parse.compares": "The code of every `@example` against the Lua parser.",
    "check.example-does-not-parse.why": "An example is the part of the documentation people copy; one that is not valid Lua fails in the reader's hands.",
    "check.feature-module-missing.compares": "The `Module:` bullet of every feature description against the files and modules of the tree.",
    "check.feature-module-missing.why": "The bullet is the way from a feature to its code and back; a stale one points a reader at a file that is gone.",
    "check.file-holds-many-modules.compares": "The module identities one file declares against the one identity the map can give a file.",
    "check.file-holds-many-modules.why": "The map attaches functions, requires and findings to a file; with several modules in one file it cannot say which of them they belong to.",
